      "id": 1,
      "text": "Red Cross, North Carolina, was incorporated on August 1, 2002, as residents wanted to keep the area agricultural and rural.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Cross%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the slick red clay that made early travel difficult before roads were paved.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofredcross.com/history",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dan Hinson built one of Stanly County’s largest stores at the town’s crossing in the early 1900s, and the building still stands today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofredcross.com/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1945, community members founded Red Cross Baptist Church, adding a key landmark to the town’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofredcross.com/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The original white wooden store was replaced in 1969 with the brick building that residents see today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
